issue.description:
Refine the existing Bitcoin gallery card with a small layout/order change and a simple static time-range selector. Keep the implementation deliberately lightweight and fully static.

## Overall direction

* Move the full-width Bitcoin price card so it appears immediately after the Chat + Recent activity row.
* Remove the historical source/date caption currently shown beneath the chart.
* Replace the current standalone `1Y` badge with a simple tab-style range selector:
  * 1Y
  * 3Y
  * 5Y
* Keep all Bitcoin price/history data static and hard-coded.
* Do not call any API and do not introduce live market data, refresh logic, network behavior, or a crypto SDK.

## 1. Reposition the Bitcoin card

Move the Bitcoin card lower in the Cards gallery so the sequence becomes:

* Chat + Recent activity row
* Bitcoin card
* Data table
* then the remaining existing gallery content in its current order

Requirements:

* preserve the Chat and Recent activity side-by-side pairing;
* keep the Bitcoin card full-width;
* do not change any other card order unless strictly required to insert Bitcoin at this position;
* preserve current responsive behavior and narrow-width stacking.

## 2. Remove the source/date caption

Remove the visible caption beneath the Bitcoin chart:

`Historical first-of-month BTC/USD, Jan 1, 2025 – Jan 1, 2026. Source: Coinbase via FRED.`

Do not replace it with alternate provenance copy in the card UI.

If provenance is still useful for implementation/audit purposes, keep it in code comments, test fixtures, phase evidence, or another non-UI location as appropriate rather than rendering it to the user.

## 3. Replace the 1Y badge with range tabs

Replace the current single `1Y` pill/badge with a compact tab/segmented selector containing:

* 1Y
* 3Y
* 5Y

Use existing accepted shadcn tab/toggle/segmented-control patterns already available in the project where appropriate.

Behavior:

* one range is active at a time;
* 1Y can remain the default active range;
* selecting 3Y or 5Y swaps the displayed static dataset and corresponding headline price/change figures;
* no network request is triggered;
* no persistence is required;
* the selector is local to this card.

Do not over-engineer this into a market-data control system.

## 4. Static datasets only

Use hard-coded static BTC/USD history for all three ranges.

Requirements:

* 1Y uses a static representative dataset for approximately one completed year;
* 3Y uses a static representative dataset spanning approximately three years;
* 5Y uses a static representative dataset spanning approximately five years;
* each range should use enough points to create a believable line shape without excessive density;
* values may be sampled at a sensible fixed interval such as monthly or another simple consistent cadence;
* displayed headline price and percentage change should derive from the selected hard-coded dataset endpoints;
* do not use runtime fetches, APIs, SDKs, websockets, background refresh, or live pricing;
* do not add credentials or network permissions.

The intent is a visual/reference component, not a trading or live-market feature.

## 5. Preserve existing card design

Preserve:

* Bitcoin/BTC title treatment;
* icon treatment;
* current full-width card structure;
* line + dots chart style;
* no grid;
* no x-axis labels;
* no y-axis labels;
* no legend;
* semantic/chart token usage;
* light/dark behavior;
* current responsive containment.

Do not add:

* trading controls;
* buy/sell actions;
* volume;
* OHLC/candlesticks;
* toolbars;
* extra financial metadata;
* API status indicators.

## 6. Accessibility and interaction

* range selector must be keyboard accessible;
* active range must be programmatically and visually distinguishable;
* preserve visible focus states;
* chart update should not cause layout shift beyond the line shape itself;
* ensure selected range remains readable in light/dark mode.

## 7. Boundaries

This is a contained presentation/component update.

Do not change:

* Theme v3;
* import/export;
* persistence/history;
* Design Command;
* mutation operations;
* public registry;
* unrelated gallery cards;
* current Bitcoin card dependency footprint.

No new dependency or network behavior should be introduced for this ticket.

## Acceptance

* Bitcoin card appears immediately below the Chat + Recent activity row.
* Chat and Recent activity remain paired side-by-side.
* Bitcoin remains full-width.
* Existing source/date caption below the chart is removed.
* Current single 1Y badge is replaced with 1Y / 3Y / 5Y tabs or equivalent segmented control.
* 1Y is the default active range.
* Switching between 1Y, 3Y, and 5Y updates the chart using only hard-coded static datasets.
* Headline price and percentage figures update consistently with the selected static dataset.
* No API, runtime fetch, SDK, live refresh, credentials, or network permission is introduced.
* Existing chart styling, semantic tokens, light/dark behavior, and responsive layout remain intact.
* No unrelated gallery order or system behavior changes.
